SUMMARY:Women's and Men's Combined Breakfast (Assembly Room)
DESCRIPTION:At the Women’s Breakfast on Saturday\, November 14\, Tim Crist will discuss the research discoveries behind his book\, New Englanders in a New Land\, published by Rutgers University Press. In the book\, Tim describes the way Congregationalists settled Newark in the 17th century and how they managed relationships with Native Americans and handled the question of slavery. \nReviewers have commended Tim’s “impressive\, pioneering research” and called the book “absorbing” in the way he “skillfully underscores the complexity of New Jersey’s origins by demonstrating how Newark’s leaders challenged the proprietary system in their quest to expand the New England model of godly authority and town self-government.” \nThis program is open to everybody. \nInformation about Tim’s book is available at: https://www.rutgersuniversitypress.org/new-englanders-in-a-new-land/9781978846883 \nCover image: https://www.rutgersuniversitypress.org/media/catalog/product/9/7/9781978846906.jpg
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/womens-and-mens-combined-breakfast-assembly-room/
LOCATION:Assembly Room
CATEGORIES:All Church Events,All Events,Featured Events,Small Groups
ORGANIZER;CN="Union Congregational Event":MAILTO:contact@unioncong.org
END:VEVENT
